          "path": "notes/mandolin-history/The Physics of the Mandolin.md",
          "before": "The Baroque [[notes/mandolin-history/The Baroque Mandolin and Regional Varieties|Milanese mandolin]] used six courses of gut, not four of metal. Gut's linear density at the same diameter is roughly **half** that of phosphor-bronze. If we naively swap to steel without rebuilding the top, the bridge load shoots up:\n- [[references::notes/mandolin-history/The Baroque Mandolin and Regional Varieties]] — the gut-string era",
